      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "8d2cef38-aa91-5168-9b5c-d2de6aeffd9a",
        ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186110756-draft/plots/d3e5c5130457db0acc662c8966f961b8d06373a25fa10af1eb6ec4de4fdd5592.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{11}$, use the Pythagorean identity to find $\\sec \u03b8$.",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "e74a2734-2707-53c1-8e65-1d3058d98c73",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "3b8cab82-e47b-53e6-ac3c-5ec560441250",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{2\\sqrt{226}}{113}"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "46ad45f6-ed2b-5de1-a89e-8f02c8bc4fd5",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{11\\sqrt{2}}{4}"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "57f90f31-48f5-5641-8018-1e2dd3ff745d",
